{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2207","id":5270201031,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOiDixw","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2207","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2207.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2207.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2207","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2207/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2207/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2207/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/0d82e65bc5be13443e83b6ccc7d1e2149f823242","number":2207,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-2177: ten tsconfig files drop the two options TypeScript 7 removes (a form change, not a proven cure)","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs KS-2177\nRefs KS-1398\n\nTicket: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-2177/ks-1398-step-one-l5-tsconfig-cleanup-that-also-works-on-typescript-5\n\n## What this changes\n\nKS-1398 step one, lane L5 (TypeScript 7 preparation). TypeScript 7 removes `moduleResolution: node` and `baseUrl`. This PR edits ten `tsconfig.json` files under `Blockchain/Dev` and adds a docs fragment pair. It changes no TypeScript version, no `package.json`, no lock, no baseline and no test file.\n\n- **moduleResolution (5 files, all `module: commonjs`):** `packages/shared`, `services/billing`, `services/nft-certificate`, `services/shared`, `services/wallet-connector` lose the `\"moduleResolution\": \"node\"` line. The earlier lane text said node16 or bundler; neither compiles for a commonjs file (TS5110, TS5095, reproduced on tsc 5.9.3) and either would need a `module` change, which changes emit. Under commonjs, TypeScript 5 resolves as node10 without the line, which is what `node` meant.\n- **baseUrl (5 files):** `frontend/admin`, `frontend/issuer`, `frontend/verifier`, `mobile/secuura-app`, `services/vc-issuer` lose `\"baseUrl\": \".\"`, and every `paths` value that was not relative gains `./` (deleting `baseUrl` alone fails with TS5090). Admin, issuer, verifier: `vendor/shared/src/*`. Mobile: eight `src/...` values. vc-issuer: two `node_modules/@secuura/shared/dist/...` values.\n- **types:** no `types` array is added. A TypeScript 7.0.2 scratch run shows no missing-global error (TS2304, TS2582, TS2593, TS2688) on the packages measured.\n- **Docs:** one fragment per page (`Projects Documents/fragments/{flow,cheat}/KS-2177-tsconfig-drops-the-two-options-typescript-7-removes.html`).\n\nServices whose `tsconfig.json` changed and what is left in them (for the work that adds `tsconfig.test.json` files, which extend these): `services/billing` and `services/wallet-connector` lose only the `moduleResolution` line; `services/vc-issuer` loses `baseUrl` and its `paths` values gain `./`, and its `tsconfig.test.json` extends it.\n\nThis is a form change, not a proven cure for the TypeScript 7 flip.\n\n## Test Evidence\n\nDevelop `1247e1af3c20`, branch cut on it. TypeScript 5.9.3 in the tree; Node v26.8.1 (not an LTS line); Apple M2, shared with other sessions; 2026-11-12 (UTC).\n\n**Touched:** the ten `tsconfig.json` files above (18 lines added, 28 removed) and the two fragment files.\n\n**Ran (before the edit, then after it, same commands, equal results):**\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tsc --noEmit` exit code and diagnostics, 9 packages | rc 0, 0 errors | equal 9 of 9 |\n| sorted `tsc --listFiles`, 9 packages | 1,519 / 813 / 675 / 431 / 568 / 576 / 653 / 1,232 / 449 files | equal 9 of 9 |\n| emitted tree (scratch `--outDir`), 6 emitting packages | 364 / 52 / 84 / 52 / 44 / 42 files | byte for byte equal, 638 of 638 files |\n| the three frontends' own `npm run build`, `dist/` | 20 / 57 / 13 files | byte for byte equal, 90 of 90 files |\n| vite determinism control | two runs of the unedited tree identical on all three | n/a |\n| `npm run build` of shared, billing, nft-certificate, services/shared, wallet-connector, vc-issuer, api-gateway, auth, referral | rc 0 | rc 0 |\n| `npm run check:test-types` (ratchet) | rc 0; auth 41 baseline errors, api-gateway 25, vc-issuer 0, security 0, m365-integration 0; 0 new, 0 stale | equal; no baseline file changed |\n| unit tests | shared 80 of 81 files (1,622 of 1,623 tests), billing 20 of 20 (377), nft-certificate 38 of 38 (241), services/shared 9 of 9 (45), wallet-connector 11 of 11 (76), vc-issuer 28 of 28 (842), frontend/issuer 1 of 3 files (4 passed, 16 failed) | equal in all seven |\n| `npm run audit:locks`, `npm run audit:gate` | n/a | rc 0 and rc 0 (no lock is touched) |\n| `docs-fragments.mjs check` | n/a | OK; a planted unclosed `<div>` turned it red (rc 1), restored by sha256, green again |\n\nThe reds in the unit-test row were red before this change: `wallet-signature` in packages/shared (KS-278) and two test files in frontend/issuer.\n\n**Planted controls that fired:** one byte changed in a copy of an emitted file is reported (363 of 364 equal); a type error planted in a scratch copy of a vc-issuer test file turns `check.cjs` red (rc 1, two new errors), and after restoring the file (sha256 equal) it is green.\n\n**TypeScript 7.0.2 in a scratch copy (a measurement, not a gate; nothing installed in this tree):**\n\n| | Before the edit | After the edit |\n|---|---|---|\n| packages/shared, billing, nft-certificate, services/shared, wallet-connector | TS5108 x1 each | rc 0 on four; billing rc 1 with TS6059 (its `include` reaches `../../shared/types`, outside the inferred `rootDir`) |\n| services/vc-issuer | TS5090 x2, TS5102 x1 | rc 0, 0 errors |\n| frontend admin, issuer, verifier | TS5102 x1, TS5090 x1 each | rc 0, 0 errors |\n\nWith the six services' test files included, no run shows a missing-global error; the errors that appear are codes TypeScript 5.9.3 reports on the same files, plus one more TS6059 in billing. The TS6059 in billing is a `rootDir` decision for the version flip and is not changed here.\n\n**NOT run / not covered:** the mobile app (nothing installed in `mobile/secuura-app`, so no `tsc` and no tests; the `paths` edit there is a form change; Expo 54.0.31's base config and @expo/cli 54.0.21's Metro resolver were read from the registry packages, not run); the frontends' Docker image builds (they build `vendor/shared`); the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6); TypeScript 7 on the frontends' test files and on the other 35 packages; `services/billing`'s TS6059.\n\n**What `baseUrl` also did:** it let a bare import such as `from 'src/x'` resolve from the package root. A git grep for bare `src/` and `vendor/` imports finds 0 in the five packages (the alias form `from '@/` finds 133 in admin), and a planted bare import compiles with `baseUrl` and fails without it.\n\n**Migrations and config:** none. No environment variable, no manifest, no lock.\n\n**Pre-push hook:** \"[pre-push] Blockchain/Dev changes detected → running preflight gate\", then \"PREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\" Legs 3, 4 and 8 skipped (the local stack was not up); leg 14: 127 shell suites passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1381 s); leg 16: five services, 0 new. This is not a pass; it says which legs ran.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T02:23:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T02:23:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"341add5b41809b99f1e9be8c239deab5f3369c65","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-2177-ks-1398-step-one-l5-tsconfig-cleanup-that","ref":"feature/ks-2177-ks-1398-step-one-l5-tsconfig-cleanup-that","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":true,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":fal